3312, "input": 44699, "output": 166}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 47934, "other": 423, "system": 31529, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 40680}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 134963}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "2450495e-6763-5a6b-a2cf-f9a00367469a", "at": 1795676383.0567112, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23895, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "9d34c58a9690fffdacc00ee245bff626", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "3f773f99-d8ba-5d98-9ac1-6a28c32279fa", "at": 1795676383.0697474, "until": 1795676384.2302866, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23896, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "9d34c58a9690fffdacc00ee245bff626", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_011FgDHakza6BRku92JSYWG7", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/repo; forge api 'repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline' | python3 -c \" import sys,json,base64;d=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode() i=t.find('## Venue frame');print(t[:200]);print(t[i:i+1800]…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/repo; forge api 'repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,base64;d=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode()\ni=t.find('## Venue frame');print(t[:200]);print(t[i:i+1800])\""]], "output": "```console\n# Outline (revision 5, after idea-review #5; revision 4 was after idea-review #3, venue #4 and the first full results of analysis, `experiment-repo`#5, results-v1) — story-repo\n\nWorking from: `Brief` \n## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\nNeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item is checked against the evidence.\n\n## 0. The paper in one paragraph\nEvaluating an LLM on a full benchmark is costly, so we run it on n ≪ N items and predict its full score. Existing methods (anchor points, tinyBenchmarks, metabench, assessor, active acquisition) use the score matrix of *source models* to pick items and fit a *latent model* of the target; they are judged mostly on held-out models that resemble the sources. We cast the problem as **finite-population estimation of a mean of N unknown 0/1 values with a free covariate (the source matrix)**. That frame separates what the sources can buy — **variance reduction** — from what must be controlled by design — **bias**. We (i) test, on 13\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "66e57a66-2acf-5df1-884d-12ca21992e6e", "at": 1795676384.0538545, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 23911, "layer": "wor